The CUDA Qwen3.5 model (vllm/models/qwen3_5/nvidia, #51012) builds its GDN layers with
fused_gdn_gated_rms_norm, so serving calls that kernel instead of the FLA layer norm that
qwen_triton_warmup warms. Its ROWS_PER_BLOCK constexpr and its num_tokens specialization both
follow the token count, and warmup never compiles them: on an RTX 4090 the JIT monitor logged
_fused_gdn_gated_rms_norm_kernel with ROWS_PER_BLOCK=2 compiling during the first request whose
prefill chunk held 257-512 tokens. This warms one token count per (specialization class, rows per
block) pair through the layer's own wrapper, with z strided out of a packed qkvz buffer as in
serving, so the quantized-output variant is chosen the same way out_proj chooses it. Upstream main
moved the kernel to vllm/models/qwen3_5/common/ and still does not warm it.

Kind: fix
What: warm the fused GDN gated norm the CUDA Qwen3.5 path calls, so a mid-size prefill chunk (257-512 tokens
  on a 4090; the band follows the SM count) no longer compiles it during a request
Upstream: none; upstream main has the same gap
Cut-against: 0.34.0
Retires-when: upstream's Qwen warmup covers fused_gdn_gated_rms_norm

